How can I use Java code to analyze a given text and extract the most frequent words? Here is an example text:
String text = "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The dog slept all day.";
I want to use this Java code to help me analyze the text:
Map<String, Integer> wordCountMap = new HashMap<String, Integer>();
String[] words = text.split("\\W+");
for (String word : words) {
    if (wordCountMap.containsKey(word)) {
        wordCountMap.put(word, wordCountMap.get(word) + 1);
    } else {
        wordCountMap.put(word, 1);
    }
}
Can you modify this Java code to extract the top 5 most frequent words from the given text?

output:
Yes, here's a modified version of the Java code that extracts the top 5 most frequent words from the given text:
```
String text = "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The dog slept all day.";
// Create a map to store word frequency
Map<String, Integer> wordCountMap = new HashMap<String, Integer>();
// Split text into words and count frequency
String[] words = text.split("\\W+");
for (String word : words) {
    if (wordCountMap.containsKey(word)) {
        wordCountMap.put(word, wordCountMap.get(word) + 1);
    } else {
        wordCountMap.put(word, 1);
    }
}
// Sort the map by value in descending order
List<Map.Entry<String, Integer>> sortedList = new ArrayList<>(wordCountMap.entrySet());
sortedList.sort(Map.Entry.<String, Integer>comparingByValue().reversed());
// Extract the top 5 most frequent words
List<String> topWords = new ArrayList<>();
for (int i = 0; i < 5 && i < sortedList.size(); i++) {
    topWords.add(sortedList.get(i).getKey());
}
// Print the top 5 most frequent words
System.out.println("Top 5 most frequent words:");
for (String word : topWords) {
    System.out.println(word + ": " + wordCountMap.get(word));
}
```
This code sorts the map by value in descending order, then extracts the top 5 most frequent words and prints them along with their frequency.

