How can I enhance the efficiency of Go in automating the data entry process and reduce the risk of errors in managing employee data while also ensuring compliance with privacy regulations? 
[Go code] Here is a sample code that can automate the data entry process in Go:
package main
import (
	"encoding/csv"
	"fmt"
	"os"
)
func main() {
	// Open the CSV file for writing
	file, err := os.Create("employee_data.csv")
	if err != nil {
		fmt.Println("Error:", err)
		return
	}
	defer file.Close()
	// Create a CSV writer
	writer := csv.NewWriter(file)
	defer writer.Flush()
	// Write the header row
	header := []string{"Employee Name", "Employee ID", "Hourly Rate", "Hours Worked", "Date of Birth", "Address", "Phone Number", "Emergency Contact"}
	err = writer.Write(header)
	if err != nil {
		fmt.Println("Error:", err)
		return
	}
	// Add employee data to the CSV file
	data := [][]string{
		{"John Doe", "123", "15.00", "40", "01/01/1990", "123 Main St.", "555-555-5555", "Jane Doe"},
		{"Jane Smith", "456", "20.00", "35", "02/02/1995", "456 Elm St.", "444-444-4444", "Bob Smith"},
		{"Bob Johnson", "789", "18.50", "45", "03/03/1980", "789 Oak St.", "333-333-3333", "Sarah Johnson"},
	}
	for _, row := range data {
		err := writer.Write(row)
		if err != nil {
			fmt.Println("Error:", err)
			return
		}
	}
	fmt.Println("Data successfully written to employee_data.csv")
} 
This code not only includes the employee name, ID, hourly rate, and hours worked, but also the employee's date of birth, address, phone number, and emergency contact. By ensuring compliance with privacy regulations, automating the data entry process with Go can further minimize the risk of errors and save time in managing employee data.

