There are several open-source natural language processing libraries available that can be used for this task, such as NLTK (Natural Language Toolkit) in Python or Stanford CoreNLP in Java. These libraries provide pre-trained models and tools for identifying the tense of a sentence.
Here's an example of how to use the Stanford CoreNLP library in MATLAB to identify the tense of a sentence:
```
% Add the Stanford CoreNLP library to the MATLAB path
javaaddpath('/path/to/stanford-corenlp.jar');
