How can we implement a Swift program that solves a set of equations for x, y, and z, and uses object-oriented programming principles to create classes for solving the equations and modeling a library system? 
First, we will create a function called "solveEquations" that takes in the coefficients of the equations as parameters and returns the solutions for x, y, and z. We will use object-oriented programming principles by encapsulating the function in a class called "EquationSolver". 
Next, we will create a subclass called "MatrixEquationSolver" that inherits from "EquationSolver" and overrides the "solveEquations" method to solve the equations using matrices. We will test both classes with the given set of equations to ensure they produce the same solutions.
To model a library system, we will create a class called "LibrarySystem" that has methods to add books and authors to the library, as well as search for books by author or title. We will use object-oriented programming principles by encapsulating the class in a module called "Library" and implementing the class as a singleton.
Here is an example implementation:
[Swift code]
class EquationSolver {
    func solveEquations(a: Int, b: Int, c: Int, d: Int, e: Int, f: Int) -> (x: Double, y: Double, z: Double) {
        // Solve the equations using math formulas
        let denominator = a*e - b*d
        let x = Double(c*e - b*f) / Double(denominator)
        let y = Double(a*f - c*d) / Double(denominator)
        let z = Double(d*b - a*e) / Double(denominator)
        return (x, y, z)
    }
}
class MatrixEquationSolver: EquationSolver {
    override func solveEquations(a: Int, b: Int, c: Int, d: Int, e: Int, f: Int) -> (x: Double, y: Double, z: Double) {
        // Solve the equations using matrices
        let coefficients = [[Double(a), Double(b), Double(-1)], [Double(d), Double(e), Double(-1)], [Double(-3), Double(2), Double(1)]]
        let results = [Double(-c), Double(-f), Double(7)]
        let matrix = Matrix(coefficients)
        let inverse = try! matrix.inverse()
        let solutions = inverse * Matrix(results).transposed()
        return (solutions[0, 0], solutions[1, 0], solutions[2, 0])
    }
}
class Library {
    static let shared = Library()
    private var books = [String: [String]]()
    private init() {}
    func addBook(title: String, author: String) {
        if books[author] == nil {
            books[author] = []
        }
        books[author]?.append(title)
    }
    func searchBooksByAuthor(author: String) -> [String] {
        return books[author] ?? []
    }
    func searchBooksByTitle(title: String) -> [String] {
        var result = [String]()
        for (author, books) in books {
            if books.contains(title) {
                result.append(author)
            }
        }
        return result
    }
}
