To find synonyms for a given word in Java, you can use a library like WordNet. WordNet is a lexical database that groups English words into sets of synonyms called synsets. Here's an example Java code that uses the WordNet library to find synonyms for the word "benevolence":
```
import edu.mit.jwi.*;
import edu.mit.jwi.item.*;
import edu.mit.jwi.morph.*;
public class SynonymsExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // initialize WordNet
        String wnhome = System.getenv("WNHOME");
        String path = wnhome + File.separator + "dict";
        URL url = new URL("file", null, path);
        IDictionary dict = new Dictionary(url);
        dict.open();
        // find synonyms for "benevolence"
        IIndexWord idxWord = dict.getIndexWord("benevolence", POS.NOUN);
        List<IWordID> wordIDs = idxWord.getWordIDs();
        List<String> synonyms = new ArrayList<String>();
        for (IWordID wordID : wordIDs) {
            IWord word = dict.getWord(wordID);
            ISynset synset = word.getSynset();
            for (IWord w : synset.getWords()) {
                synonyms.add(w.getLemma());
            }
        }
        // use a synonym to rephrase a sentence
        String sentence = "Her benevolence towards others is truly inspiring.";
        String synonym = synonyms.get(0);
        String rephrased = sentence.replace("benevolence", synonym);
        System.out.println("Synonyms for 'benevolence': " + synonyms);
        System.out.println("Rephrased sentence: " + rephrased);
    }
}
```
This code initializes WordNet and finds synonyms for "benevolence" using the `getIndexWord` method. It then loops over the synsets associated with the word and adds each synonym to a list. Finally, it uses the first synonym in the list to rephrase a sentence.
